// An index assignment evaluates the object, the index and the value, in this
// order, before it checks the object. Assignment to a String is a halting
// fault (spec/04-semantics.md, Halting Faults), so the value is evaluated
// first: the program prints INDEX and VALUE, then halts. The effects before
// the fault bind (spec/README.md, Conformance).
fun i() { print "INDEX"; return 0; }
fun v() { print "VALUE"; return "x"; }
var s = "abc";
s[i()] = v();
print "after";

// STATUS: error
// CHECK: INDEX
// CHECK: VALUE
